estion bank missing']);","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\api\\data.php","text":"<?php\ndeclare(strict_types=1);\n\nrequire_once __DIR__ . '/../lib/db.php';\n\n$id = preg_replace('/[^A-Za-z0-9\\-_]/', '', $_GET['id'] ?? '');\n$row = $id !== '' ? exam_get($id) : null;\n\nif (!$row || $row['status'] !== 'done') {\n    http_response_code(404);\n    header('Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8');\n    echo json_encode(['ok' => false, 'error' => 'Not found or not ready']);\n    exit;\n}\n\n$file = exam_dir($id) . '/questions.json';\nif (!is_file($file)) {\n    http_response_code(500);\n    header('Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8');\n    echo json_encode(['ok' => false, 'error' => 'Question bank missing']);\n    exit;\n}\n\nheader('Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8');\nheader('Cache-Control: no-store');\necho (string)file_get_contents($file);\nexit;","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":27,"totalLines":27,"truncated":false}},"title":"xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\api\\data.php","time":{"start":1789887246003,"end":1789887246010}},"id":"prt_0bd97ee2a001sWsA3hGqkyipwT","sessionID":"ses_f42685812ffeYBxHvYBLR3HFUo","messageID":"msg_0bd97df900019ilgMQGkqOvOXk"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789887246291,"sessionID":"ses_f42685812ffeYBxHvYBLR3HFUo","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_1f8f87090a734869ab3168b9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\enaxqoqxb74s4g\\questions.json","limit":120},"output":"<path>C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\enaxqoqxb74s4g\\questions.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:     \"title\": \"IAS 2 Reviewer\",\n3:     \"subject\": \"Information Assurance and Security 2 (ITAS311-T) - 3rd Year 1st Sem\",\n4:     \"summary\": \"Comprehensive interactive examination covering the reviewer's six lessons: post-audit activities including the exit interview, data analysis, audit reports and presentation of findings (Lessons 3 and 5); log information and security controls from security logging through IDS detection methods, layered defense, NAC, host isolation and system hardening (Lesson 4); the risk management process of identification, assessment, response and monitoring (Lesson 6); business continuity management with RTO, RPO, MTD, BIA, plan review and testing (Lesson 7); and backing up data with incident response preparation, the three-phase response model, post-incident review, documentation and reporting (Lesson 8).\",\n5:     \"chapters\": [\n6:         {\n7:             \"chapterId\": \"ch1\",\n8:             \"title\": \"Post-Audit Activities\",\n9:             \"description\": \"Covers the definition of post-audit activities, the exit interview (participants, purpose, preparation, advantages and limitations), the five-step data analysis process, the audit report format and qualities, and the presentation of findings, drawing on Lessons 3 and 5.\",\n10:             \"questions\": [\n11:                 {\n12:                     \"id\": \"ch1-q01\",\n13:                     \"question\": \"Which statement best describes post-audit activities?\",\n14:                     \"choices\": [\n15:                         \"Steps performed to plan and schedule the audit engagement before fieldwork begins.\",\n16:                         \"Actions after an audit to review, analyze, document, and communicate its results.\",\n17:                         \"Controls installed by management to limit access during field testing work.\",\n18:                         \"Procedures used to collect evidence while the audit is in progress.\"\n19:                     ],\n20:                     \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n21:                     \"explanation\": \"Post-audit activities are performed after the audit has been conducted to review, analyze, document, and communicate the results.\"\n22:                 },\n23:                 {\n24:                     \"id\": \"ch1-q02\",\n25:                     \"question\": \"When is an exit interview normally held?\",\n26:                     \"choices\": [\n27:                         \"Before the audit scope and objectives are agreed with the audited entity.\",\n28:                         \"Immediately after the final audit report has been released.\",\n29:                         \"At the conclusion of audit fieldwork, when necessary.\",\n30:                         \"During the initial planning stage of the audit.\"\n31:                     ],\n32:                     \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n33:                     \"explanation\": \"An exit interview is a meeting held at the conclusion of audit fieldwork, when necessary, before the final report is released.\"\n34:                 },\n35:                 {\n36:                     \"id\": \"ch1-q03\",\n37:                     \"question\": \"What does the Prepare objective of an exit interview accomplish?\",\n38:                     \"choices\": [\n39:                         \"It lets the client respond and comment before the final report is issued.\",\n40:                         \"It guarantees that any disputed findings will be removed from the report.\",\n41:                         \"It transfers responsibility for corrective actions to the audit team.\",\n42:                         \"It prevents the audited entity from reviewing the audit evidence.\"\n43:                     ],\n44:                     \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n45:                     \"explanation\": \"The Prepare objective allows the audit client to provide responses and comments before the final report is issued.\"\n46:                 },\n47:                 {\n48:                     \"id\": \"ch1-q04\",\n49:                     \"question\": \"Which sequence represents the post-audit reporting flow in the reference?\",\n50:                     \"choices\": [\n51:                         \"Draft report review, exit interview, management responses, final audit report.\",\n52:                         \"Exit interview, draft report review, final audit report, management responses.\",\n53:                         \"Management responses, final report, exit interview, draft report review.\",\n54:                         \"Exit interview, management responses, draft report review, final audit report.\"\n55:                     ],\n56:                     \"correctAnswer\": 3,\n57:                     \"explanation\": \"The reference sequence is audit fieldwork, exit interview, management responses and comments, draft report review, then final audit report.\"\n58:                 },\n59:                 {\n60:                     \"id\": \"ch1-q05\",\n61:                     \"question\": \"What is the general purpose of the exit interview?\",\n62:                     \"choices\": [\n63:                         \"To discuss findings and clarify concerns before the report is finalized.\",\n64:                         \"To finish all the field testing and evidence collection work for the audit.\",\n65:                         \"To publish the final audit report to the stakeholders.\",\n66:                         \"To set the scope and objectives of the next audit.\"\n67:                     ],\n68:                     \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n69:                     \"explanation\": \"The exit interview gives the auditor and audited entity a chance to discuss findings, clarify concerns, and establish common understanding before the report is finalized.\"\n70:                 },\n71:                 {\n72:                     \"id\": \"ch1-q06\",\n73:                     \"question\": \"What is the purpose of audit team participation in the exit interview?\",\n74:                     \"choices\": [\n75:                         \"To approve the corrective actions that the management proposes.\",\n76:                         \"To audit the meeting as an independent observer.\",\n77:                         \"To present and explain the findings and lead the discussion.\",\n78:                         \"To record the minutes for the audit client's records.\"\n79:                     ],\n80:                     \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n81:                     \"explanation\": \"The audit team, such as the lead auditor, presents and explains the audit findings and facilitates the discussion.\"\n82:                 },\n83:                 {\n84:                     \"id\": \"ch1-q07\",\n85:                     \"question\": \"What is the main role of the audited entity's management in the exit interview?\",\n86:                     \"choices\": [\n87:                         \"To independently verify the audit team's testing methods.\",\n88:                         \"To review the findings and provide context and explanations.\",\n89:                         \"To decide which findings appear in the final report.\",\n90:                         \"To complete the remaining field work on behalf of the auditors.\"\n91:                     ],\n92:                     \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n93:                     \"explanation\": \"Management of the audited entity reviews the findings, provides explanations or additional context, and responds to the issues identified.\"\n94:                 },\n95:                 {\n96:                     \"id\": \"ch1-q08\",\n97:                     \"question\": \"Who may attend as other participants in an exit interview?\",\n98:                     \"choices\": [\n99:                         \"Personnel who are selected by the lead auditor during the meeting.\",\n100:                         \"Regulators required to approve every exit interview.\",\n101:                         \"Consultants hired to conduct the follow-up audit.\",\n102:                         \"People invited by the client to add information or perspective.\"\n103:                     ],\n104:                     \"correctAnswer\": 3,\n105:                     \"explanation\": \"Other participants are individuals invited by the audit client to supply relevant information, clarification, or perspective about the audited processes or findings.\"\n106:                 },\n107:                 {\n108:                     \"id\": \"ch1-q09\",\n109:                     \"question\": \"Which two questions guide auditors when using the exit interview to close information gaps?\",\n110:                     \"choices\": [\n111:                         \"What failed and who is to blame?\",\n112:                         \"Why was the issue missed and how was it discovered?\",\n113:                         \"Who will provide the missing information and when?\",\n114:                         \"How much will the fix cost and who will pay?\"\n115:                     ],\n116:                     \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n117:                     \"explanation\": \"Auditors use the exit interview to identify missing information by asking who is responsible for providing it and when it can be expected.\"\n118:                 },\n119:                 {\n120:                     \"id\": \"ch1-q10\",\n\n(Showing lines 1-120 of 2453. Use offset=121 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n    \"title\": \"IAS 2 Reviewer\",\n    \"subject\": \"Information Assurance and Security 2 (ITAS311-T) - 3rd Year 1st Sem\",\n    \"summary\": \"Comprehensive interactive examination covering the reviewer's six lessons: post-audit activities including the exit interview, data analysis, audit reports and presentation of findings (Lessons 3 and 5); log information and security controls from security logging through IDS detection methods, layered defense, NAC, host isolation and system hardening (Lesson 4); the risk management process of identification, assessment, response and monitoring (Lesson 6); business continuity management with RTO, RPO, MTD, BIA, plan review and testing (Lesson 7); and backing up data with incident response preparation, the three-phase response model, post-incident review, documentation and reporting (Lesson 8).\",\n    \"chapters\": [\n        {\n            \"chapterId\": \"ch1\",\n            \"title\": \"Post-Audit Activities\",\n            \"description\": \"Covers the definition of post-audit activities, the exit interview (participants, purpose, preparation, advantages and limitations), the five-step data analysis process, the audit report format and qualities, and the presentation of findings, drawing on Lessons 3 and 5.\",\n            \"questions\": [\n                {\n                    \"id\": \"ch1-q01\",\n                    \"question\": \"Which statement best describes post-audit activities?\",\n                    \"choices\": [\n                        \"Steps performed to plan and schedule the audit engagement before fieldwork begins.\",\n                        \"Actions after an audit to review, analyze, document, and communicate its results.\",\n                        \"Controls installed by management to limit access during field testing work.\",\n                        \"Procedures used to collect evidence while the audit is in progress.\"\n                    ],\n                    \"correctAnswer\": 1,","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\enaxqoqxb74s4g\\questions.json","text":"{\n    \"title\": \"IAS 2 Reviewer\",\n    \"subject\": \"Information Assurance and Security 2 (ITAS311-T) - 3rd Year 1st Sem\",\n    \"summary\": \"Comprehensive interactive examination covering the reviewer's six lessons: post-audit activities including the exit interview, data analysis, audit reports and presentation of findings (Lessons 3 and 5); log information and security controls from security logging through IDS detection methods, layered defense, NAC, host isolation and system hardening (Lesson 4); the risk management process of identification, assessment, response and monitoring (Lesson 6); business continuity management with RTO, RPO, MTD, BIA, plan review and testing (Lesson 7); and backing up data with incident response preparation, the three-phase response model, post-incident review, documentation and reporting (Lesson 8).\",\n    \"chapters\": [\n        {\n            \"chapterId\": \"ch1\",\n            \"title\": \"Post-Audit Activities\",\n            \"description\": \"Covers the definition of post-audit activities, the exit interview (participants, purpose, preparation, advantages and limitations), the five-step data analysis process, the audit report format and qualities, and the presentation of findings, drawing on Lessons 3 and 5.\",\n            \"questions\": [\n                {\n                    \"id\": \"ch1-q01\",\n                    \"question\": \"Which statement best describes post-audit activities?\",\n                    \"choices\": [\n                        \"Steps performed to plan and schedule the audit engagement before fieldwork begins.\",\n                        \"Actions after an audit to review, analyze, document, and communicate its results.\",\n                        \"Controls installed by management to limit access during field testing work.\",\n                        \"Procedures used to collect evidence while the audit is in progress.\"\n                    ],\n                    \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n                    \"explanation\": \"Post-audit activities are performed after the audit has been conducted to review, analyze, document, and communicate the results.\"\n                },\n                {\n                    \"id\": \"ch1-q02\",\n                    \"question\": \"When is an exit interview normally held?\",\n                    \"choices\": [\n                        \"Before the audit scope and objectives are agreed with the audited entity.\",\n                        \"Immediately after the final audit report has been released.\",\n                        \"At the conclusion of audit fieldwork, when necessary.\",\n                        \"During the initial planning stage of the audit.\"\n                    ],\n                    \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n                    \"explanation\": \"An exit interview is a meeting held at the conclusion of audit fieldwork, when necessary, before the final report is released.\"\n                },\n                {\n                    \"id\": \"ch1-q03\",\n                    \"question\": \"What does the Prepare objective of an exit interview accomplish?\",\n                    \"choices\": [\n                        \"It lets the client respond and comment before the final report is issued.\",\n                        \"It guarantees that any disputed findings will be removed from the report.\",\n                        \"It transfers responsibility for corrective actions to the audit team.\",\n                        \"It prevents the audited entity from reviewing the audit evidence.\"\n                    ],\n                    \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n                    \"explanation\": \"The Prepare objective allows the audit client to provide responses and comments before the final report is issued.\"\n                },\n                {\n                    \"id\": \"ch1-q04\",\n                    \"question\": \"Which sequence represents the post-audit reporting flow in the reference?\",\n                    \"choices\": [\n                        \"Draft report review, exit interview, management responses, final audit report.\",\n                        \"Exit interview, draft report review, final audit report, management responses.\",\n                        \"Management responses, final report, exit interview, draft report review.\",\n                        \"Exit interview, management responses, draft report review, final audit report.\"\n                    ],\n                    \"correctAnswer\": 3,\n                    \"explanation\": \"The reference sequence is audit fieldwork, exit interview, management responses and comments, draft report review, then final audit report.\"\n                },\n                {\n                    \"id\": \"ch1-q05\",\n                    \"question\": \"What is the general purpose of the exit interview?\",\n                    \"choices\": [\n                        \"To discuss findings and clarify concerns before the report is finalized.\",\n                        \"To finish all the field testing and evidence collection work for the audit.\",\n                        \"To publish the final audit report to the stakeholders.\",\n                        \"To set the scope and objectives of the next audit.\"\n                    ],\n                    \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n                    \"explanation\": \"The exit interview gives the auditor and audited entity a chance to discuss findings, clarify concerns, and establish common understanding before the report is finalized.\"\n                },\n                {\n                    \"id\": \"ch1-q06\",\n                    \"question\": \"What is the purpose of audit team participation in the exit interview?\",\n                    \"choices\": [\n                        \"To approve the corrective actions that the management proposes.\",\n                        \"To audit the meeting as an independent observer.\",\n                        \"To present and explain the findings and lead the discussion.\",\n                        \"To record the minutes for the audit client's records.\"\n                    ],\n                    \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n                    \"explanation\": \"The audit team, such as the lead auditor, presents and explains the audit findings and facilitates the discussion.\"\n                },\n                {\n                    \"id\": \"ch1-q07\",\n                    \"question\": \"What is the main role of the audited entity's management in the exit interview?\",\n                    \"choices\": [\n                        \"To independently verify the audit team's testing methods.\",\n                        \"To review the findings and provide context and explanations.\",\n                        \"To decide which findings appear in the final report.\",\n                        \"To complete the remaining field work on behalf of the auditors.\"\n                    ],\n                    \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n                    \"explanation\": \"Management of the audited entity reviews the findings, provides explanations or additional context, and responds to the issues identified.\"\n                },\n                {\n                    \"id\": \"ch1-q08\",\n                    \"question\": \"Who may attend as other participants in an exit interview?\",\n                    \"choices\": [\n                        \"Personnel who are selected by the lead auditor during the meeting.\",\n                        \"Regulators required to approve every exit interview.\",\n                        \"Consultants hired to conduct the follow-up audit.\",\n                        \"People invited by the client to add information or perspective.\"\n                    ],\n                    \"correctAnswer\": 3,\n                    \"explanation\": \"Other participants are individuals invited by the audit client to supply relevant information, clarification, or perspective about the audited processes or findings.\"\n                },\n                {\n                    \"id\": \"ch1-q09\",\n                    \"question\": \"Which two questions guide auditors when using the exit interview to close information gaps?\",\n                    \"choices\": [\n                        \"What failed and who is to blame?\",\n                        \"Why was the issue missed and how was it discovered?\",\n                        \"Who will provide the missing information and when?\",\n                        \"How much will the fix cost and who will pay?\"\n                    ],\n                    \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n                    \"explanation\": \"Auditors use the exit interview to identify missing information by asking who is responsible for providing it and when it can be expected.\"\n                },\n                {\n                    \"id\": \"ch1-q10\",","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":120,"totalLines":2453,"truncated":true}},"title":"xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\enaxqoqxb74s4g\\questions.json","time":{"start":1789887246259,"end":1789887246288}},"id":"prt_0bd97eedb001UVLzyqhRuod9oP","sessionID":"ses_f42685812ffeYBxHvYBLR3HFUo","messageID":"msg_0bd97df900019ilgMQGkqOvOXk"}}
